Project-CarpeDiem
=================

Getting started
---------------

To get started with CarpeDiem, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the CarpeDiem trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/Project-CarpeDiem/android.git -b seventeen --git-lfs
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync
```
CarpeDiem is based on LineageOS `lineage-24.0` (tracked on branch `seventeen`). See `snippets/carpediem.xml`
for the repositories CarpeDiem forks; everything else tracks upstream.

Build Flags
-----------
```
# Maintainer Name
CARPEDIEM_MAINTAINER := "YourInput" (Default: Unknown)

# Whether Including GMS Prebuilts
WITH_GMS := true/false (Default: false)

# GMS Flavor
GMS_MAKEFILE := gms_mini.mk/gms_full/gms_pico (Default: gms_mini.mk)

# Official Build
CARPEDIEM_OFFICIAL := true/false (Default: false)
```

Custom Commands
---------------
Source the tree first (`. build/envsetup.sh`), then:
```
# Configure: carpe <device> [user|userdebug|eng] [gms|mini|full|pico|va]
# Default package is vanilla. GMS variants: gms/mini, full, pico.
carpe Galaxian userdebug gms

# Build: cb [-b|-fb|-br] [-j<num>] [user|eng|userdebug] [device]
# -b: bacon, -fb: fastboot package, -br: brunch. Plain `cb` runs `m`.
cb -b -j$(nproc --all)
```

Setup Environment:
------------------
Navigate to the root directory of Project-CarpeDiem:
```
cd path/to/source
```
Run the environment setup script:
```
. build/envsetup.sh
```
Build Configuration:
--------------------
Choose your device configuration:
```
lunch lineage_$device-$buildtype
```
Replace $device with your device codename and $buildtype with your prefered build type (user, userdebug or eng).
Compilation:
------------
Start the compilation process:
```
m bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

Submitting patches
------------------
Patches are always welcome! Please submit them via GitHub pull requests
against the `seventeen` branch of the relevant `Project-CarpeDiem` repository.
